cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "AdaRpGAN: A Self-Tuning GAN Training Framework with Adaptive Gradient Penalty and Dynamic Critic Scheduling"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-06-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yourusername/adarppgan"
url: "https://github.com/yourusername/adarppgan"
abstract: >-
  AdaRpGAN is a PyTorch-based GAN training framework that automatically tunes the
  gradient-penalty weight (γ) and discriminator update frequency (n_critic) during
  training using two closed-loop control signals: an exponential moving average of
  Lipschitz violation for γ, and rolling-window loss variance for n_critic. Built on
  a Relativistic GAN backbone, AdaRpGAN achieves a 32.8% FID improvement on CIFAR-10
  over the fixed-γ baseline with zero additional compute cost.
keywords:
  - GAN
  - generative-adversarial-network
  - deep-learning
  - pytorch
  - adaptive-training
  - gradient-penalty
  - relativistic-GAN
  - self-tuning
